(Sweet, well-behaved kid.)

297
00:22:16,920 --> 00:22:19,720
(But the Su family
clearly favored the boy.)

298
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:23,160
(I figured that spoiled boy)

299
00:22:23,590 --> 00:22:25,960
(was stealing my fried eggs.)

300
00:22:26,830 --> 00:22:27,960
(So the next day,)

301
00:22:28,720 --> 00:22:31,680
(I decided to teach the kid a lesson.)

302
00:23:20,640 --> 00:23:21,200
Squat down.

303
00:23:31,640 --> 00:23:32,680
You did it yesterday too?

304
00:23:35,240 --> 00:23:36,160
S-Sorry.

305
00:23:36,960 --> 00:23:38,030
I was starving.

306
00:23:38,480 --> 00:23:39,830
I thought it was your brother.

307
00:23:41,480 --> 00:23:42,310
Too salty, huh?

308
00:23:44,590 --> 00:23:45,160
Rinse.

309
00:23:46,440 --> 00:23:47,240
Toss the egg.

310
00:24:00,110 --> 00:24:00,880
Spit here.

311
00:24:10,350 --> 00:24:10,880
Squat down.

312
00:24:23,070 --> 00:24:23,750
Mr. Gu.

313
00:24:25,400 --> 00:24:26,400
Let me pay you back.

314
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:28,920
Can I pay you back over time?

315
00:24:29,640 --> 00:24:30,480
You don't have to.

316
00:24:32,880 --> 00:24:35,590
If you're hungry, come tell me.

317
00:24:37,440 --> 00:24:38,680
I'll fry you some eggs.

318
00:24:41,440 --> 00:24:43,000
I'll make you two right now.

319
00:24:46,880 --> 00:24:48,790
Will they be that salty again?

320
00:24:56,830 --> 00:24:57,640
(From then on,)

321
00:24:58,680 --> 00:25:00,350
(every night when I made eggs,)

322
00:25:00,350 --> 00:25:01,240
(I'd make two extra)

323
00:25:01,720 --> 00:25:02,640
(for Su Lin.)

324
00:25:04,030 --> 00:25:05,240
(She was such a good kid.)

325
00:25:06,510 --> 00:25:09,400
(After eating, she'd wash every dish)

326
00:25:09,440 --> 00:25:11,030
(and put them away.)

327
00:25:12,030 --> 00:25:13,310
(She knew I was learning English,)

328
00:25:13,960 --> 00:25:14,920
(so she'd help me.)

329
00:25:19,640 --> 00:25:20,000
(Paris
The Louvre)

330
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:21,960
(Italy
Venice)

331
00:25:22,440 --> 00:25:23,790
Such a thoughtful kid.

332
00:25:24,680 --> 00:25:26,160
She'd write Chinese

333
00:25:26,200 --> 00:25:27,270
under every English word.

334
00:25:28,200 --> 00:25:30,440
(Su Lin, Ordinary Student)
If nothing happened to her,

335
00:25:31,310 --> 00:25:32,310
but she didn't go home,

336
00:25:33,880 --> 00:25:35,070
where could she be?

337
00:26:02,550 --> 00:26:03,240
Captain.

338
00:26:03,790 --> 00:26:05,160
Why didn't you go home and rest?

339
00:26:05,830 --> 00:26:07,750
We haven't found the person below.

340
00:26:08,270 --> 00:26:09,640
I couldn't sleep anyway.

341
00:26:13,480 --> 00:26:14,240
Major Crimes Two.

342
00:26:15,640 --> 00:26:16,680
Sun Hui's roommate?

343
00:26:17,830 --> 00:26:21,200
Ever since what happened to Sun Hui,

344
00:26:22,510 --> 00:26:23,270
I can't sleep.

345
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:25,000
I keep having dreams.

346
00:26:26,960 --> 00:26:28,920
My cousin just graduated
and starts an internship.

347
00:26:29,200 --> 00:26:30,880
I'm moving in with her.

348
00:26:31,640 --> 00:26:33,270
While packing last night,

349
00:26:33,440 --> 00:26:34,640
I found this box.

350
00:26:35,920 --> 00:26:37,350
Sun Hui left it behind.

351
00:26:44,790 --> 00:26:45,830
(Bath Ticket)
Bath ticket.

352
00:26:50,110 --> 00:26:51,270
A People's Park ticket.

353
00:26:55,350 --> 00:26:57,550
(Receipt Stub)
A FOREVER bicycle receipt.

354
00:26:58,440 --> 00:26:59,750
Sun Hui had a bike?

355
00:27:00,270 --> 00:27:02,240
The purchase date

356
00:27:02,240 --> 00:27:03,830
(Receipt Stub)
was the weekend before she disappeared.

357
00:27:05,350 --> 00:27:06,030
She just bought it?

358
00:27:07,480 --> 00:27:08,640
We already

359
00:27:08,640 --> 00:27:10,960
rode her bus route to work.

360
00:27:11,110 --> 00:27:12,510
It was packed at rush hour.

361
00:27:12,750 --> 00:27:14,640
A bike commute makes perfect sense.

362
00:27:15,160 --> 00:27:16,480
But if that's true,

363
00:27:17,070 --> 00:27:18,000
she wouldn't go missing

364
00:27:18,030 --> 00:27:19,960
near the bus stop.

365
00:27:22,550 --> 00:27:23,720
Find that bike.

366
00:27:23,790 --> 00:27:25,110
Sun Hui's roommate

367
00:27:25,110 --> 00:27:26,240
gave us a major lead.

368
00:27:27,310 --> 00:27:28,510
(Receipt Stub)
Here's the bike receipt

369
00:27:28,720 --> 00:27:30,070
from before she disappeared.

370
00:27:30,550 --> 00:27:31,550
But we checked.

371
00:27:32,240 --> 00:27:32,960
The bike

372
00:27:32,960 --> 00:27:34,000
is gone too.

373
00:27:34,590 --> 00:27:36,030
So she probably

374
00:27:36,030 --> 00:27:37,160
rode it out that day.

375
00:27:37,440 --> 00:27:38,640
A brand-new bike

376
00:27:38,920 --> 00:27:40,200
wouldn't just vanish.

377
00:27:41,160 --> 00:27:42,680
The killer probably

378
00:27:42,720 --> 00:27:43,270
dumped it.

379
00:27:43,400 --> 00:27:44,920
If we find that bike,

380
00:27:45,480 --> 00:27:46,070
maybe

381
00:27:46,070 --> 00:27:47,720
the handlebars or seat still have

382
00:27:47,750 --> 00:27:48,680
the killer's prints

383
00:27:49,070 --> 00:27:50,310
or some other trace.

384
00:27:51,550 --> 00:27:53,510
Focus on her usual route.

385
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:54,960
Check used-bike shops.

386
00:27:55,720 --> 00:27:56,590
And scrapyards.

387
00:27:56,750 --> 00:27:58,270
Even if the bike was stripped,

388
00:27:58,790 --> 00:28:00,480
find every part.

389
00:28:01,160 --> 00:28:02,750
The killer has brutally murdered

390
00:28:02,750 --> 00:28:03,960
at least two women.

391
00:28:04,110 --> 00:28:05,550
He could strike again anytime.

392
00:28:05,960 --> 00:28:06,920
Every day we wait

393
00:28:07,070 --> 00:28:08,200
puts us further behind.

394
00:28:08,550 --> 00:28:11,110
We need him in custody fast.

395
00:28:12,550 --> 00:28:13,960
What about the person taken below?

396
00:28:14,240 --> 00:28:15,110
Any progress?

397
00:28:15,310 --> 00:28:16,310
Still searching below.

398
00:28:16,640 --> 00:28:18,240
The tunnels are a maze.

399
00:28:18,510 --> 00:28:19,960
They're extremely hard to search.

400
00:28:20,200 --> 00:28:21,350
So far, nothing

401
00:28:21,350 --> 00:28:22,480
useful has turned up.

402
00:28:25,000 --> 00:28:26,070
I know how hard

403
00:28:26,070 --> 00:28:26,750
the search is.

404
00:28:27,110 --> 00:28:28,590
Keep working it.

405
00:28:28,790 --> 00:28:29,440
Wang.

406
00:28:29,750 --> 00:28:31,510
Stay on this bike lead.

407
00:28:31,640 --> 00:28:32,510
Don't let it go.

408
00:28:32,920 --> 00:28:34,310
Follow this lead,

409
00:28:34,750 --> 00:28:35,510
and we'll

410
00:28:35,550 --> 00:28:36,550
smoke the killer out.

411
00:29:03,790 --> 00:29:04,750
Let me help.

412
00:29:06,440 --> 00:29:08,750
We can split the work.

413
00:29:17,960 --> 00:29:19,550
Collect recyclables, sell them.

414
00:29:20,480 --> 00:29:22,240
I can help you make money too.

415
00:29:26,270 --> 00:29:27,750
Back home,

416
00:29:28,030 --> 00:29:29,830
I always helped my mom with chores.

417
00:29:31,510 --> 00:29:32,830
I have a great memory.

418
00:29:33,310 --> 00:29:34,720
Just show me the route a few times,

419
00:29:34,830 --> 00:29:35,880
and I'll know the way.

420
00:29:36,640 --> 00:29:37,310
Then...

421
00:29:37,590 --> 00:29:39,270
Then I can go on my own.

422
00:29:41,480 --> 00:29:42,160
At least

423
00:29:43,030 --> 00:29:44,750
I can help sort things.

424
00:29:48,920 --> 00:29:49,310
I...

425
00:29:50,030 --> 00:29:51,720
I can do lots of other work too.

426
00:29:52,920 --> 00:29:53,440
Hey.

427
00:30:17,880 --> 00:30:18,510
Mom.

428
00:30:18,880 --> 00:30:19,640
Why the rush?

429
00:30:19,790 --> 00:30:21,750
The teacher said
our performance passes were due.

430
00:30:22,400 --> 00:30:23,200
I forgot.

431
00:30:26,790 --> 00:30:27,640
Is one enough?

432
00:30:28,200 --> 00:30:28,830
Yep.

433
00:30:29,760 --> 00:30:36,720
(Chaobei Youth Recitation Contest
Performance Pass)

434
00:30:42,400 --> 00:30:42,920
Mom.

435
00:30:43,960 --> 00:30:45,270
Why don't you wait here?

436
00:30:45,440 --> 00:30:46,440
No rehearsal today.

437
00:30:46,550 --> 00:30:47,720
Just gotta turn in my pass.

438
00:30:51,350 --> 00:30:53,510
I won't be home for dinner tonight.

439
00:30:53,720 --> 00:30:54,640
I'm meeting coworkers.

440
00:30:55,440 --> 00:30:56,270
Eat without me.

441
00:30:59,110 --> 00:31:00,480
Doesn't Li always invite you out?

442
00:31:00,790 --> 00:31:02,110
You should return the favor.

443
00:31:04,640 --> 00:31:05,550
Take her to dinner.

444
00:31:09,070 --> 00:31:09,640
Here.

445
00:31:10,790 --> 00:31:11,400
Enough?

446
00:31:12,240 --> 00:31:12,750
Yeah.

447
00:31:16,000 --> 00:31:16,480
Let's go.

448
00:31:31,680 --> 00:31:33,510
Their class used to do pretty poorly.

449
00:31:34,110 --> 00:31:35,590
But they've improved lately.

450
00:31:35,720 --> 00:31:36,270
Right?

451
00:31:36,550 --> 00:31:37,160
Ms. Wang.

452
00:31:39,240 --> 00:31:39,960
Mr. Zhou.

453
00:31:45,400 --> 00:31:46,750
Can I ask you a favor?

454
00:31:47,640 --> 00:31:48,200
What is it?

455
00:31:49,160 --> 00:31:50,960
(Zhou Xijie, Artistic Director(Poet))
On this poster, could you remove

456
00:31:51,530 --> 00:31:52,480
(Reciters: Ma Na, Yang Le, etc.)
the word "poet"?

457
00:31:55,750 --> 00:31:56,830
What? Why?

458
00:31:56,880 --> 00:31:58,030
It doesn't feel right.

459
00:31:59,270 --> 00:32:00,480
No need to be modest.

460
00:32:01,000 --> 00:32:03,240
Your work's been published many times.

461
00:32:03,550 --> 00:32:04,640
Then you're a poet.

462
00:32:04,680 --> 00:32:05,400
To me, poet

463
00:32:05,440 --> 00:32:06,400
is a professional title.

464
00:32:06,720 --> 00:32:09,400
So it really doesn't belong on a poster.

465
00:32:10,440 --> 00:32:13,440
I think it suits you perfectly.

466
00:32:14,110 --> 00:32:15,240
Look at the poster.

467
00:32:15,720 --> 00:32:18,200
The Little Mermaid rests in water,

468
00:32:18,590 --> 00:32:21,110
watching the sun rise in the distance.

469
00:32:21,830 --> 00:32:22,830
A scene like this

470
00:32:23,000 --> 00:32:24,720
just needs a poem to complete it.

471
00:32:25,400 --> 00:32:26,110
Your poem-

472
00:32:26,110 --> 00:32:27,240
Ms. Wang,

473
00:32:27,590 --> 00:32:28,720
I don't think it fits.

474
00:32:28,960 --> 00:32:30,510
Poetry is too personal.

475
00:32:30,830 --> 00:32:32,350
So I really don't think "poet"

476
00:32:32,550 --> 00:32:33,680
should be on the poster.

477
00:32:34,070 --> 00:32:34,590
Of course,

478
00:32:35,000 --> 00:32:36,480
if you could remove my name too,

479
00:32:36,550 --> 00:32:37,270
even better.

480
00:32:38,550 --> 00:32:39,480
Thanks, Ms. Wang.

481
00:33:03,550 --> 00:33:04,880
This girl's father

482
00:33:05,070 --> 00:33:07,000
is a well-known local businessman,

483
00:33:07,240 --> 00:33:08,070
Ma Dongchen.

484
00:33:08,590 --> 00:33:09,200
Mr. Ma.

485
00:33:09,350 --> 00:33:10,550
Su, that's settled then.

486
00:33:11,590 --> 00:33:13,440
I'll let you know when it's done.

487
00:33:13,720 --> 00:33:14,550
Bye, Mr. Ma.

488
00:33:14,750 --> 00:33:15,480
What class?

489
00:33:15,790 --> 00:33:16,510
Hospitality.

490
00:33:16,720 --> 00:33:18,200
Did you get along with Su Lin?

491
00:33:19,550 --> 00:33:20,550
Who's Su Lin?

492
00:33:31,960 --> 00:33:32,720
Who's this?

493
00:33:33,750 --> 00:33:34,880
Hey, Gu.

494
00:33:35,880 --> 00:33:36,920
I checked everywhere.

495
00:33:37,270 --> 00:33:39,110
Hospitals and shelters downtown,

496
00:33:39,350 --> 00:33:40,960
no girl named Su Lin.

497
00:33:41,720 --> 00:33:42,480
Nowhere?

498
00:33:45,750 --> 00:33:46,830
Thanks, Liu.

499
00:33:47,240 --> 00:33:47,720
No problem.

500
00:34:33,030 --> 00:34:34,670
Cooking, Mr. Gu?

501
00:34:47,110 --> 00:34:47,800
Just got back?

502
00:34:49,070 --> 00:34:49,710
Yeah.

503
00:34:54,360 --> 00:34:56,000
No one was home all afternoon, right?

504
00:34:56,670 --> 00:34:57,150
Right.

505
00:35:03,150 --> 00:35:04,030
All afternoon,

506
00:35:04,670 --> 00:35:06,800
the public phone there
rang five or six times.

507
00:35:08,110 --> 00:35:08,840
Really?

508
00:35:10,440 --> 00:35:11,840
Could your daughter have called?

509
00:35:24,510 --> 00:35:25,710
Maybe.

510
00:35:33,440 --> 00:35:34,440
But at that hour,

511
00:35:35,710 --> 00:35:38,030
she should've been in class.

512
00:35:38,360 --> 00:35:39,230
It probably wasn't her.

513
00:35:42,800 --> 00:35:44,400
Right. If Lin had called,

514
00:35:44,440 --> 00:35:46,400
she would've called at night.

515
00:35:54,960 --> 00:35:56,630
That phone rang all afternoon.

516
00:35:56,630 --> 00:35:58,480
I worried someone had an emergency,

517
00:35:58,510 --> 00:35:59,440
so I came to tell you.

518
00:36:01,280 --> 00:36:02,400
This afternoon,

519
00:36:02,400 --> 00:36:04,070
we had to go out.

520
00:36:04,590 --> 00:36:05,550
Her dad

521
00:36:06,630 --> 00:36:07,590
hurt his leg.

522
00:36:07,590 --> 00:36:09,480
I took him to get his bandage changed.

523
00:36:11,230 --> 00:36:12,360
Hurt? Is it bad?

524
00:36:13,590 --> 00:36:15,440
Doctor says even when it heals,

525
00:36:15,440 --> 00:36:16,880
he'll be disabled.

526
00:36:17,840 --> 00:36:19,030
He'll limp for life.

527
00:36:20,710 --> 00:36:21,630
That bad?

528
00:36:23,760 --> 00:36:25,070
If it happened at work,

529
00:36:25,190 --> 00:36:26,280
that's a work accident.

530
00:36:26,670 --> 00:36:28,440
The site can be held responsible.

531
00:36:29,280 --> 00:36:31,230
Which site? Did they compensate him?

532
00:36:33,000 --> 00:36:34,710
He still needs that job.

533
00:36:34,710 --> 00:36:35,630
The boss...

534
00:36:36,510 --> 00:36:38,190
The boss is

535
00:36:38,550 --> 00:36:39,550
a decent guy.

536
00:36:39,590 --> 00:36:41,670
He said once he's better,

537
00:36:41,670 --> 00:36:43,070
he can go back to work.

538
00:36:47,480 --> 00:36:48,710
About compensation,

539
00:36:48,920 --> 00:36:50,880
if you need help,

540
00:36:51,110 --> 00:36:52,230
I can ask around for you.

541
00:36:53,030 --> 00:36:54,440
No, no. The boss...

542
00:36:54,920 --> 00:36:55,510
The boss

543
00:36:55,510 --> 00:36:58,590
already took care of everything.

544
00:37:04,800 --> 00:37:05,550
Thank you.

545
00:37:12,550 --> 00:37:15,230
Sounds like a good boss.

546
00:37:29,920 --> 00:37:30,550
Off to work?

547
00:37:32,350 --> 00:37:39,230
(Dingsheng Construction Crew)

548
00:38:00,840 --> 00:38:02,880
5351671.

549
00:38:03,590 --> 00:38:05,190
1671.

550
00:38:05,230 --> 00:38:07,230
5351671.

551
00:38:21,840 --> 00:38:22,400
Hello?

552
00:38:22,920 --> 00:38:23,590
Mr. He.

553
00:38:24,360 --> 00:38:25,070
It's Gu.

554
00:38:25,880 --> 00:38:26,590
(Gu.)

555
00:38:26,670 --> 00:38:27,190
(What's up?)

556
00:38:27,800 --> 00:38:28,510
Quick question.

557
00:38:29,230 --> 00:38:31,590
Your son works at
Chaobei No. 3 Construction, right?

558
00:38:32,030 --> 00:38:32,480
(Yeah.)

559
00:38:32,590 --> 00:38:33,320
(Chaobei No. 3.)

560
00:38:33,440 --> 00:38:33,880
(Why?)

561
00:38:35,000 --> 00:38:37,190
I need him to ask around for me.

562
00:38:38,000 --> 00:38:41,320
There's a crew called Dingsheng.

563
00:38:42,000 --> 00:38:44,320
What company are they working for now?

564
00:38:45,840 --> 00:38:46,630
Specifically,

565
00:38:47,550 --> 00:38:48,760
lately,

566
00:38:49,320 --> 00:38:52,070
has there been an accident on that job?

567
00:38:53,670 --> 00:38:54,840
Anyone get hurt?

568
00:38:55,030 --> 00:38:56,400
(Sure. I'll ask and let you know.)

569
00:38:56,400 --> 00:38:56,920
Okay.

570
00:38:57,190 --> 00:38:57,710
(I'll call.)

571
00:38:57,710 --> 00:38:58,230
Thanks.

572
00:38:58,920 --> 00:39:00,110
(No need. We're old friends.)

573
00:39:00,320 --> 00:39:00,880
(Gotta go.)

574
00:39:55,920 --> 00:39:56,590
You're awake.

575
00:39:58,550 --> 00:39:59,440
Newspapers are there.

576
00:39:59,670 --> 00:40:00,550
I tied them up.

577
00:40:01,070 --> 00:40:02,110
We'll keep them there.

578
00:40:06,030 --> 00:40:06,920
These sacks here

579
00:40:06,960 --> 00:40:08,280
are full of plastic bottles.

580
00:40:09,070 --> 00:40:10,280
The cans are over there.

581
00:40:25,440 --> 00:40:27,150
I tied up all the cardboard too.

582
00:40:28,070 --> 00:40:29,230
That way,

583
00:40:29,280 --> 00:40:30,880
we can take it out in stacks.

584
00:40:31,230 --> 00:40:32,230
It'll be a lot easier.

585
00:40:37,510 --> 00:40:38,230
Well?

586
00:40:39,320 --> 00:40:41,000
Can I go out with you now?

587
00:41:40,550 --> 00:41:42,550
Come on. Let's go together.

588
00:41:43,110 --> 00:41:43,920
Wait for me.

589
00:42:32,400 --> 00:42:32,920
Take it.

590
